      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-lanka-kanda-0081",
      "sequence": 936,
      "meaning": "Brahmā, the gods, siddhas and sages watch the colourful battle from aerial cars, with Śiva and Umā among them. Champions on both sides are drunk on the flavour of combat, though the monkeys are victorious through Rāma’s strength. Warriors challenge one another, crush opponents to earth, cut, seize and dash them down, strike heads with severed heads, tear open bellies and wrench away arms. Bears bury demons and heap sand upon them. The opposing heroes look like many angry forms of Death.",
