      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-lanka-kanda-0082",
      "sequence": 937,
      "meaning": "Rāvaṇa rushes forward in supreme fury as monkeys meet him roaring. They hurl trees, boulders and mountains together, but the missiles shatter instantly against his adamant body. Unmoved in his planted chariot and mad with battle, he darts about crushing monkey champions. Bears and monkeys flee crying to Aṅgada, Hanumān and Raghubīra for protection from the villain who devours like Death. Seeing the monkeys scatter, Rāvaṇa strings all ten bows and fits his arrows.",
