    {
      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-lanka-kanda-0083",
      "sequence": 938,
      "meaning": "Lakṣmaṇa challenges Rāvaṇa to look at the death appointed for him instead of killing monkeys and bears, and says he has long sought his son’s killer. Rāvaṇa releases a terrible arrow, but Lakṣmaṇa cuts it into a hundred pieces. He similarly reduces millions of weapons to sesame-sized fragments, then shoots down Rāvaṇa’s chariot and driver, pierces all ten foreheads with a hundred arrows each, and drives another hundred into his chest. Rāvaṇa falls senseless, revives, and hurls the spear once given him by Brahmā.",
