      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-lanka-kanda-0084",
      "sequence": 939,
      "meaning": "After an omitted transition in the pinned witness, the text resumes with Hanumān bracing on one knee rather than falling from Rāvaṇa’s blow. He regains his balance in fury and fells the demon like a mountain struck by lightning. When Rāvaṇa revives and praises the monkey’s immense strength, Hanumān condemns his own prowess because the enemy still lives. He takes Lakṣmaṇa to Rāma, astounding Rāvaṇa. Rāma reminds his brother that he devours Death and protects the gods. Lakṣmaṇa rises at those words; the dreadful spear returns to the sky, and he eagerly takes bow and arrows and confronts the enemy again.",
