      "sequence": 940,
      "meaning": "Vibhīṣaṇa swiftly tells Rāma that Rāvaṇa is performing a sacrifice which, if completed, will keep the wretch from dying. At dawn the Lord sends Hanumān, Aṅgada and the other champions to destroy it. They leap into Laṅkā and enter Rāvaṇa’s palace without fear. Enraged to see him performing the rite after shamelessly fleeing battle, Aṅgada kicks him and accuses him of coming home to pose in meditation. Fixed upon his object, Rāvaṇa does not look up.",
