      "sequence": 941,
      "meaning": "Terrible evil omens attend Rāvaṇa: vultures wheel above and settle upon his heads. Ruled by death, he heeds no one and orders the war drums sounded. The vast demon army of elephants, chariots, infantry and cavalry races toward the Lord like moths into fire. The gods pray that Rāma not prolong the sport that has caused Sītā such pain. Smiling at their words, Raghubīra rises and prepares his arrows, tightly binds his matted hair with flowers woven through it, and stands dark as a raincloud with reddened eyes, armed at waist, quiver and hand with the hard Śārṅga bow.",
