    {
      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-lanka-kanda-0088",
      "sequence": 943,
      "meaning": "Ghosts, ghouls, vetālas, fierce attendants and dreadful spirits bathe in the river of blood. Crows and vultures fight over severed arms; one ghoul mocks another that even amid this abundance will not end its poverty. Groaning wounded warriors lie along the banks like dying people laid half in water. Vultures draw out entrails like anglers intent on their lines, while many corpses drift under perched birds like boats. Yoginīs collect blood in skull-cups, spectral women dance, headless fighters clap skulls like cymbals and Cāmuṇḍās sing. Packs of jackals gnash, eat, howl, gorge and swagger; millions of headless trunks stagger as fallen heads cry victory.",
      "lines": [
