      "meaning": "The gods are distressed to see the Lord fighting on foot, so Indra promptly sends his own incomparable radiant chariot with Mātali. Rāma gladly mounts; its four charming, ageless horses move with the speed of thought. Seeing Raghunātha chariot-borne, the monkeys charge with renewed strength. Unable to endure their assault, Rāvaṇa spreads an illusion that does not deceive Rāma but appears real to Lakṣmaṇa and the monkeys: they see a demon army filled everywhere with many copies of the Lord of Kosala and his younger brother.",
