      "sequence": 945,
      "meaning": "Bowing his head to the lotus feet of brahmins, Raghunātha drives the chariot. Rāvaṇa charges in wrath, roaring that he is unlike the warriors Rāma has already defeated: the world knows his name, and the guardians of the worlds are his prisoners. He belittles the deaths of Khara, Dūṣaṇa, Virādha, Vāli, the demon hosts, Kumbhakarṇa and Meghanāda, and threatens to hand Rāma to Death unless he flees. Knowing the abuse to come from one already ruled by death, the compassionate Lord laughs and concedes the truth of Rāvaṇa’s power, but tells him to stop boasting and show his manliness.",
